              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 13.3: Graph of the linear equation 4x + 3y = 12"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.431,
            0.884,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Substituting "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 0 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we get 5y = 0, that is, y = 0. So (0, 0) is a solution of the given equation. To get another solution, substitute x = 1. The corresponding value of y is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "-\\frac{2}{5}, \\mathrm{~S}0, (1, -\\frac{2}{5})"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is also a solution. In fact, we can substitute any value for x and obtain a corresponding value of y. For example, substituting "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = 5"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we obtain "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = - 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Let us represent these solutions or ordered pairs in the form of a table."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.297,
            0.558,
            0.648,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.297,
                0.558,
                0.648,
                0.642
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.652,
            0.883,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we plot the ordered pairs A (0, 0), "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { B } \\left( 1 , { \\frac { - 2 } { 5 } } \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and C (5, –2) we see that they lie on a line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
